# Windows checks files out with CRLF line endings; Linux CI runners expect LF.
# A shell script with CRLF fails on Linux with the famously unhelpful
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M". Force LF for everything the CI
# runner executes, regardless of which OS it was committed from.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
